2. CONDITIONS

2.1 Register your use.
    Before a copy of the Software (modified or not) becomes reachable by anyone other than you, whether as
    a public or private website, an intranet, a hosted service or a published copy of the code, register
    that use by opening an issue with the "Usage registration" form at

        https://github.com/mert-turkgil/SpeakingClub/issues/new?template=usage-registration.yml

    and giving:
      - your name or the name of your organisation;
      - a way to contact you;
      - the address (URL) of the deployment, or "private" / "internal" if it has none;
      - one or two sentences on how you use it.

    If you would rather not register publicly, send the same information privately to the copyright holder
    through the contact options on https://github.com/mert-turkgil. Update the registration if this
    information changes significantly.

    Running the Software only on your own computer, where nobody else can reach it (for example to try it
    out or to develop a change), does not need to be registered.

2.2 Keep the notices.
    Keep the copyright notice above and this license file in every copy, and in every substantial portion,
    of the Software.

2.3 Give credit.
    Every deployment that other people can reach must show a visible credit, for example in the footer or
    on an About or credits page, reading "Built with Almanca Konuş" (or the equivalent in the site's
    language) with a link to https://github.com/mert-turkgil/SpeakingClub.

2.4 Use your own identity.
    Do not present your deployment as the original Almanca Konuş website, or as run, endorsed or
    supervised by Suna Koç or Mert Türkgil, unless they have agreed to it in writing.


